@cc [owner:philipperolet,label:architecture] preserve-completed-backfills
Treat backfills already on `main` as completed historical records: do not delete them or change
their implementation. The only exception is work explicitly preparing the same backfill to run or
rerun.

If later application changes break a completed TypeScript backfill, add a top-level
`// @ts-nocheck` instead of adapting its implementation. If it has a dedicated test,
the test may be deleted.
